meta {
  name: 05_AuthorizationBoundaries
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  Scenario: The API rejects callers without the required authorization

    When no token is provided the estate check fails
    When no token is provided adding an administrator fails
    When another person reads the bostyrer's administrators the request fails
    When another person adds an administrator for the bostyrer the request fails
    When another person revokes an administrator for the bostyrer the request fails
    When only the write scope is used to read the request fails
    When only the read scope is used to add the request fails
    When only the read scope is used to revoke the request fails
    When the token scope is unrelated the request fails
    And the dedicated read scope grants access to the estate check
    When the party parameter is missing the request fails
    When the party parameter is not a uuid the request fails
    When the party is unknown the request fails
    When the party is one of the bostyrer's estates the request fails

    Authorization runs before the body is read, so none of the add requests here look up a
    person. 401 and 403 responses carry no problem body, so only the status is asserted.
}
